From: Artem Pelenitsyn <a.pelenitsyn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:16:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Compile the C sources of libraries with mhs

mhs compiles no C when it builds a library. It compiles the C sources of a
library when it links a program that loads the package file of the library,
from <name>-<version>/cbits beside the package file, which is where
MicroCabal installs the c-sources of a library. Cabal ignored the C sources
of libraries with a warning, and gave mhs no include directories of the
dependencies of a component, so a program calling into the C code of a
library failed to compile, as with time, which takes the time zone from C:

  fatal error: HsTime.h: No such file or directory

buildLib now copies the c-sources of a library there, beside the package
file in its build directory, and installLib copies them along with the
package file. The headers are found as with GHC: the include-dirs that the
registrations of the dependencies of a component list, which is where Cabal
installs their install-includes for every compiler, are given to mhs with
-I, which it passes on to the C compiler. See Note [MicroHs C files of
libraries]. The cc-options of an executable are now passed to mhs, with
-optc, for its own C sources.

The test MHS/CSources builds a library with C sources and a header from a
repository, into the store, and another one in place, and runs an
executable calling both.

